    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "And we are back with another edition of the Federalist Radio Hour. I'm Matt Kittle, Senior Elections Correspondent at the Federalist and your experienced Sherpa on Today's Quest for Knowledge. As always, you can email the show at radio at thefederalist.com. Follow us on acts at F-B-R-L-S-T. Make sure to subscribe wherever you download your podcast and, of course, to the premium version of our website as well. My guest today is U.S. Senator Ron Johnson, Republican representing the great and electorally powerful state of Wisconsin. Thank you, sir, for being here and joining us on this edition of the Federalist Radio Hour. Well, Matt, thanks for having me on. We've got much to talk about. You've been extremely busy. I can know and I can speak for that, having covered you in Wisconsin since your election first in 2010. You're in the middle of your third term and there is no rest for the weary, is there?",
