  {
    "episode_id": 46645,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46645.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Indeed, I wanted to talk to you and we'll delve into Wisconsin's significant role in the 2024 election, just as it played a significant role in 2020 and 2016 as a swing state. But before we do that, I wanted to get the latest information. You have been along with many colleagues, but you in particular have been investigating the assassination attempt, former President Donald Trump, the GOP's presidential candidate in the incident, of course, occurring in Butler, Pennsylvania, July 13th. First and foremost, Are you as, I don't know exactly what the word is, it's not disappointed because we know emotives and means here, but are you surprised as I am that the accomplice media in this country has so memory hold this horrifying incident that occurred before our very eyes, right before the Republican National Convention?",
