  {
    "episode_id": 46645,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46645.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "They're just not giving us the information. So finally, it was six or seven weeks after the assassination attempt, they put five individuals on administrative leave. Now, what exactly does that mean? I think they're still getting paid. I mean, are they still in the office? I mean, we really don't know. We don't know exactly which ones or what the reasons or rationale were. Again, the people they are offering us for interviews. I mean, I can't say we're fighting that they're lying to us. They just don't have much information. Again, from my standpoint, the number one person I wanted to interview was the sniper who took out crooks. They said, again, there were conspiracies floating around that the sniper had crooks in his sights for a minute or two and asked for permission to take him out and permission was denied. Now, the scene services completely denied that. I think other people that we have talked to, that does not sound plausible. But I'd like to talk to the sniper. Again, our timeline, generally timelines are in days, right? I mean, this timeline is in minutes and then in two seconds around the shooting. I mean, the snipers had a lot of time to be looking at the AGR building and trying to find some of these sites. And we know from the video, from the individual who got shot twice, I mean, to talk about. you know, coincidence. This guy shooting a video, then he gets shot twice. But his is a really interesting video because three minutes before the first shots were fired at 608. We see crux running across the top that building kind of step going up and down the right right hand part of the screen. So you can see it from the ground. I mean, if you're a sniper team, you've got a picture of crooks sent to you I think 26 minutes before the actual shooting. We have confirmed that the Secret Service lead sniper knew about that and the individual suspicious individuals around the AGI building. I mean you would think you just have your sights on the AGI building and again we're not talking to the sniper.",
