    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "Well, our nation has been so blessed. I mean, in the span of human history, it means brutality, the lack of freedom to have for a few hundred years the shining city on a hill, what America represents. It's rare. It's precious. You know, and of course we don't teach history. So I don't think enough Americans truly appreciate how unbelievably lucky we are in the Spanish human history to have what we have. But again, we're all human beings. You see affluence. You just always want more. You take things for granted. But we can't take this for granted. I mean, Venezuelans voted themselves in poverty, only took a couple of decades. We're right now going down a very dangerous path. So again, this nation has been immeasurably blessed by God, by our Creator. I hope he's looking down and I hope he I hope he blesses us again. We simply can't continue down this road of destruction that the radical left has put us on. So that's one of the reasons, Matt, I've proposed for the Republican tariffs in the Senate. We need a mission statement. What are we for? What are we willing to fight for? So I've proposed relatively simple one to fight and defeat the ideology and policies of the radical left to destroy in this country. Now, quite honestly, I'd like to have something a little more uplifting, but at this point in time, that's gotta be our mission. The radical left is destroying this country. They have gained control over all its institutions. They need to be fought and defeated. And then we can look forward to, again, rebuilding this country really in the image of our founding fathers.",
